  "thin_entity_classification_rule": {
    "contact_layer": "A: real workface/perimeter function, including the four thin cells; repartition, never relax the accepted workface.",
    "backing": "A for tip/major exterior sidewall; B for pocket wall/bulkhead/roof. A thin convex cut is not a reason to retire its functional shell.",
    "mount_block": "C for assembly bore/recess terrain slivers with no independent feature identity; retain all incident B cap, mouth and void obligations. B for a cell carrying the actual root-slot floor.",
    "distinction": "Entity tier describes why the thin entity exists. Surface tiers independently describe what its replacement must preserve. A C entity never retires an incident A/B surface."
  },
  "runtime_surface_metric": {
    "reference_target": "Only actual frozen reference-union exterior subpatches labelled A or B by the pre-geometry source atlas/predicates. Reference internal closures are never surface targets.",
    "runtime_target": "Actual union-exterior patches corresponding to A/B targets. A novel exterior closure or C-gap mouth cap adjoining the macroscopic envelope inherits the stricter adjacent A/B tier.",
    "formula": "For t in {A,B}: sup_{x in T_t} dist(x,R_t) and sup_{y in R_t} dist(y,T_t) <= the tier budget; also enforce each tier contour and normal obligations.",
    "C_exclusion": "Exclude only prelisted C subpatches in the reference-to-runtime direction. A vanished C seam has no required runtime exterior counterpart. Still-C deep cavity surfaces use local material/void checks rather than Hausdorff. Forward C exclusion requires the same frozen source-space C predicate, <=0.05mm provenance neighborhood, and no overlap with an A/B target or protected mouth/edge.",
